sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-24> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Although the localized structures found in rules 30 and 45 on repetitive backgrounds all move at the same speed and so cannot interact, preventing a rule 110-style proof, rules 30 and 45 will nevertheless turn out to be universal.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rules 30 and 45 are expected to be universal";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 11, “The Notion of Computation”; section “The Threshold of Universality in Cellular Automata” (from p. 694), p. 701. Scope: the rule 30 and rule 45 elementary cellular automata"
}
